      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Digital subtraction angiography, using a time interval difference mode in relation to a suitable mask, provides a means of showing the myocardium in every phase of the cardiac cycle. The endo- and peri-cardial contours and the thickness of the myocardium in both ventricles can be demonstrated accurately. Artifacts are usually due to displacements of the heart or to tachycardia."},
